"""Beaker-on-hotplate task: scene loading, start-up settle, the success check and the points the fixed eagle camera must see.

Plain functions and flat dicts (src/task_config.py), no classes. The arms -> pedestal -> drive -> creep-in staging sequence is NOT
here: it is the scripted source in src/staging_source.py, which uses the helpers of this file (view_points, wrap).

make_task() packages the task for the generic episode runner (src/episode_runner.py): a dictionary that says how to reset the scene, which policy
to run, how to check success and what the time limits are (see the runner's docstring for the keys). rebuild_task() is what replay calls (from the
recipe stored in a recording) to rebuild the model. run_beaker_episode() is a shorthand for tests that builds the task and runs one episode.

Reused from the repo: src.simulator.RobotSimulator (scene load, arm / finger position actuators, cameras, the
placeholder pedestal lift, the eagle camera's body) and the start-up of experiments/combined_controller.py / pedestal_lift_test.py (warm-up
with the arms held at zero, capture of the drooped pose as the resting pose, short re-settle with it held).
"""

